{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yigini/soilfer-lims/pulls/299","id":4888152132,"node_id":"PR_kwDOROLhSM8AAAABI1tIRA","html_url":"https://github.com/yigini/soilfer-lims/pull/299","diff_url":"https://github.com/yigini/soilfer-lims/pull/299.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/yigini/soilfer-lims/pull/299.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yigini/soilfer-lims/issues/299","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yigini/soilfer-lims/pulls/299/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yigini/soilfer-lims/pulls/299/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yigini/soilfer-lims/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yigini/soilfer-lims/issues/299/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yigini/soilfer-lims/statuses/457fba5cbffe4157e1c2b428800a620f131854d6","number":299,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"feat(labels): QR, Code128 and audited reprints (#208)","user":{"login":"yigini","id":32960535,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyOTYwNTM1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32960535?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yigini","html_url":"https://github.com/yigini","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yigini/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yigini/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yigini/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yigini/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yigini/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yigini/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yigini/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yigini/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yigini/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"References #208.\n\nLabels now use the exact issued sample/container identity for both QR and Code128. Sample, container and aliquot printing share one scoped server command and dialog; a reprint requires a reason before the browser print dialog opens.\n\n- Add immutable LabelPrintEvent rows with identity, issued code, count, ordinal, format, reason, actor and timestamp. SQL guards protect references, copy counts, print ordering and reprint reasons.\n- Re-read permissions, sample scope and state at print time; refuse missing, ambiguous or unsupported codes with stable 4xx codes. Keep historical issued bytes and the approved numbering authority unchanged.\n- Add the guarded additive installer, startup/entrypoint integration and all five locale catalogs. Record browser print requests truthfully, including cancellations and lost responses.\n- Document the MOD 37,36 hybrid system's adjacent-transposition limitation. Preserve physical label sizes and require larger stock when Code128 bars would otherwise be compressed below 0.19 mm.\n\nValidation:\n- Complete server suite: **375 suites / 5,702 tests passed** (2,196.411 s), with the full discovered inventory and both ordinary setup files.\n- Client production build passed; client lint passed with 0 errors and 14 existing warnings.\n- Contract and real React DOM tests cover issued-code preservation, QR/Code128 payload parity, reasoned/concurrent reprints, permissions/scope, stale dialog requests, installer preservation/refusals and strict scanner binding.\n\nWindows local validation used a retained, Git-free visible Temp fixture because hidden `.codex` paths break Jest discovery and Express file downloads. The stock assertions, scanner and complete inventory remain unchanged; only a relative testMatch CLI override was used. Exact source/build inputs and generated runtime were checked before and after; the scanner used a hash-verified read-only index copy. The disposable database was provisioned from Prisma's empty-schema SQL and ordinary CI seeds, then copied with a WAL-aware SQLite backup after the Windows ARM64 db-push engine failed.\n\nThe earlier full checkout run is retained: 370 suites passed and 5 failed (hidden-path downloads/SPA, a CRLF-converted pinned fixture, and the telemetry fixture's old 26-stage expectation). The exact pinned Git blob was restored, and telemetry now verifies all 27 stages plus refusal boundaries. Incomplete local fixture attempts are also retained. The final complete run above passed on the frozen inputs; only the documented test-generated help manifest changed, with before/after bytes retained and excluded from this commit. Repository Jest and CI configuration are unchanged.\n\nRelated follow-up: the existing preanalytic deletion handler can return a generic 500 when a RESTRICT foreign key blocks deletion. A printed RECEIVED sample is retained by the new evidence reference and may reach that existing handler path, as containers already can. This PR preserves evidence and leaves deletion authority unchanged, following the issue's scope guard.\n\nPhysical printer/scanner acceptance, deployment and actual post-deploy acceptance remain pending. Historical prints are not inferred and issued codes are never renumbered. The issue remains open.\n\nTested source: `457fba5cbffe4157e1c2b428800a620f131854d6`; tree `26a56ccb234c49d85d1d3c96374904aa239ccbe5`; parent/base `be8379745bdfae52ce46496ff26514dc7d729640`. Normal PR CI and exact-head audit are pending. No merge or deployment is authorized by this PR.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-16T12:09:28Z","updated_at":"2026-10-16T12:09:28Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"00a6b0c7fde1b8fdd586aed1774a9d3af8962ed3","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"yigini:codex/issue-208-labels","ref":"codex/issue-208-labels","repo":{"id":1155719496,"node_id":"R_kgDOROLhSA","name":"soilfer-lims","full_name":"yigini/soilfer-lims","owner":{"login":"yigini","id":32960535,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyOTYwNTM1","avatar_